  "title": "Kirby Problem 3.6",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Given a cofinal tower of covers M $\\leftarrow$ $M_1$ $\\leftarrow$ $M_2$ $\\leftarrow$ $\\cdots$, is it true that the torsion subgroups $\\operatorname{Tor}(M_{n})$ of $H_1(M_{n}, \\mathbb{Z})$ and the hyperbolic volumes $\\operatorname{vol}(M_{n})$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\log|\\operatorname{Tor}(M_n)|}{\\operatorname{vol}(M_n)}=\\frac{1}{6\\pi}\\,?\n$$",
